1
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,710
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:10,380
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:14,290
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:17,150
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:21,290
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,570
G-Guts?

7
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,730
Commander Guts?

8
00:00:27,210 --> 00:00:29,370
Is it really you, Commander Guts?

9
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,140
Commander Guts!

10
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,370
Commander Guts!

11
00:00:57,410 --> 00:00:59,490
Feel no shame about shape

12
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,410
Weather changes their phrase

13
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:05,160
Even mother will show you another way

14
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:07,540
So put your glasses on

15
00:01:07,630 --> 00:01:09,630
Nothing will be wrong

16
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:11,840
There's no blame. There's no fame

17
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,670
It's up to you

18
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:17,300
The first words should be found

19
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:20,930
Whatever holds you back

20
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:22,310
I...

21
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,430
...can...

22
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,600
I can get it off

23
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,600
Tell me what...

24
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:27,600
Tell me what...

25
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:29,440
Tell me what you want

26
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:30,520
I don't know why...

27
00:01:30,730 --> 00:01:31,520
Don't know why...

28
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,530
Don't know why you're afraid

29
00:01:33,690 --> 00:01:34,690
Tell me what...

30
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:35,650
Tell me what...

31
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:37,320
Tell me what you'd say

32
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:38,660
I don't know why...

33
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:39,740
Don't know why...

34
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:40,530
Too late...

35
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,160
It's too late

36
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:51,090
Confession

37
00:01:54,550 --> 00:01:55,630
Guts...

38
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:57,010
Guts?

39
00:01:57,010 --> 00:01:58,220
Is it possible?

40
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:00,050
The legendary commander...

41
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,470
There's no time to waste.

42
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:04,180
Don't you have a job to do?

43
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:12,900
Don't back off!

44
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,440
Get into battle formation
and launch a counterattack!

45
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:24,120
Who cares if he killed a hundred men?

46
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,290
Their numbers are small.

47
00:02:25,290 --> 00:02:27,080
Advance! Advance forward!

48
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:05,410
Those eyes...

49
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:07,080
They haven't changed.

50
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,580
It's no use. We don't stand a chance.

51
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:12,170
Damn it!

52
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:13,750
There's no choice! Retreat!

53
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,710
Don't let them get away!

54
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:19,260
Stop, don't jeopardize yourself!

55
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:20,510
But... we can't...

56
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:21,630
Guts!

57
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:24,430
What the hell, guys!

58
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:30,480
Guts!

59
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,810
So you survived all this time, Rickert?

60
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:34,940
G-Guts...

61
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,450
Commander!

62
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:44,740
Commander Guts!

63
00:03:45,410 --> 00:03:46,620
I knew it!

64
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,740
I knew you'd come back someday!

65
00:03:50,410 --> 00:03:51,290
You guys...

66
00:03:58,460 --> 00:04:00,460
There's no time to lose!

67
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,010
The enemy will return.

68
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:04,130
We must mobilize while it's dark.

69
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:05,970
Casca...

70
00:04:05,970 --> 00:04:07,220
We'll catch up later.

71
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:10,100
We should get moving now,
just like she says.

72
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:26,240
In this past year, we've been cut down
to a fifth of what we were before...

73
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:31,290
The Band of the Hawk
can no longer be called an army.

74
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:35,460
Even so, it could be worse...

75
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:40,670
Without Casca, there would
be nothing left of us at all...

76
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:45,590
On that fateful day a year ago...

77
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:51,430
We all gathered under Griffith's order.

78
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:54,850
We hadn't ridden our horses in a while.

79
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:58,110
And so we waited...
But little did we know...

80
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,450
What's taking Griffith so long?

81
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:22,000
Everybody, get down!

82
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:29,350
All of a sudden, arrows came
pouring down on us like rain.

83
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:31,640
It was the Midland army...

84
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,470
Everything was in chaos...

85
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,520
We found out only after we had escaped...

86
00:05:38,270 --> 00:05:41,070
...that Griffith had been
captured and arrested for treason.

87
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:45,610
Griffith?

88
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,610
A year ago...

89
00:05:47,610 --> 00:05:49,700
It was the day after you left.

90
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:52,450
I can't believe it...

91
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,700
The Griffith we knew...

92
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:55,620
Why?

93
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:57,790
After you left, Guts...

94
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,540
Griffith was very depressed...

95
00:06:01,710 --> 00:06:05,130
If you ask me... I think it was
because of you that Griffith...

96
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:13,560
Don't flatter yourself...

97
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:18,100
What happened to Griffith
has absolutely nothing to do with you.

98
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:19,400
Nothing.

99
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:23,940
But you should have seen
how Casca came through!

100
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:27,570
She had five serious wounds
but still led us till the end of the battle!

101
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:32,200
And that was when
we welcomed Casca as our leader.

102
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:34,620
Still, who would've thought...

103
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,540
...you'd be coming back
just when we needed you most?

104
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,710
It goes to show that
our luck hasn't run out yet.

105
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:44,040
We've been planning an operation,
and we're about to carry it out.

106
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:45,340
An operation?

107
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,550
We're going to rescue Griffith.

108
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:59,480
All the guys left here
are in dreadful shape.

109
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,940
Their hearts and bodies
are covered with wounds...

110
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:05,440
But not one of them
will even consider leaving us...

111
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,530
...even though no one's
told them they have to stay.

112
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:12,280
All we have is courage and willpower...
but in the end what can that do?

113
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:17,660
The ones who are left are Band of
the Hawk members down to the bone...

114
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:19,960
It's not Griffith we are rescuing...

115
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:24,000
It's the Band of the Hawk
that wouldn't exist without him.

116
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:31,680
It's good to be back...

117
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:34,470
Some things never change.

118
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:36,100
We're counting on you...

119
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,180
...Commander Guts.

120
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:39,890
You mean ex-Commander.

121
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:41,190
Corkus!

122
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:45,480
That bastard left us
when we needed him the most!

123
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:48,320
How can any of you
say he's one of us?

124
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,780
Corkus, that's too harsh!

125
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:53,030
You're nothing but
an outsider now, through and through!

126
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:55,660
At least make things
right, though... Got it?

127
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,160
Yeah...

128
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:58,950
I hear you.

129
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:04,830
Guts...

130
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,380
Take care of...

131
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:08,920
...Casca.

132
00:08:10,670 --> 00:08:13,050
That fateful day a year ago...

133
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:16,800
Casca spent three long days and
nights lingering on the brink of death...

134
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:20,520
In the throes of nightmares
she cried out, over and over...

135
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,020
...for Griffith...

136
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:25,100
...and you.

137
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:36,870
She's pushing herself
more than she'll ever let on...

138
00:08:37,410 --> 00:08:38,280
So...

139
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:40,290
Do something about it, will you?

140
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:42,790
The rest of us just aren't up to the task.

141
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,360
Quite impressive...

142
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:18,490
There's still life in those eyes of yours.

143
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:29,130
Don't worry.

144
00:09:29,130 --> 00:09:32,840
I'm avoiding your vitals,
so you're not in any mortal danger.

145
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:38,340
The king has ordered me to ensure
you live at least another three years.

146
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:48,230
Youth can be so frightening...

147
00:09:48,230 --> 00:09:51,150
...or perhaps I should say
it's a marvel to behold!

148
00:09:52,770 --> 00:09:58,660
Still, man must live in line with his
standing, even a hero as great as you.

149
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:00,910
But it seems you were quite misguided!

150
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:08,540
I've been wondering about
this unusual charm you're wearing.

151
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:12,630
But if it has no power
to protect you, it's utterly useless!

152
00:10:42,410 --> 00:10:44,030
Come with me. I want to talk to you.

153
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,330
What do you want?

154
00:10:53,210 --> 00:10:53,880
Take your stance!

155
00:11:02,510 --> 00:11:03,930
Hey, wait!

156
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:06,310
I said wait!

157
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,020
What the hell?

158
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:20,150
Hey, cut it out!

159
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:21,410
Don't patronize me!

160
00:11:21,410 --> 00:11:22,030
Draw your sword!

161
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,580
What the hell's wrong with you?

162
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:30,460
We haven't seen
each other in a year, damn it...

163
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:33,210
...and the first thing
you do is attack me?

164
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:38,090
Why the hell did you come back now?

165
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:40,970
It's your fault!

166
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,720
You destroyed everything!

167
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,600
It's all your fault!

168
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:47,760
My fault?

169
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,930
That's right...

170
00:11:48,930 --> 00:11:50,060
Griffith and...

171
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:51,350
The Band of the Hawk...

172
00:11:51,350 --> 00:11:52,980
Everything...

173
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:54,900
It all went to hell because of you!

174
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:55,770
I did this?

175
00:11:55,770 --> 00:11:56,400
How?

176
00:11:57,770 --> 00:11:59,440
Because you left us...

177
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:01,860
Because you left Griffith!

178
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:07,370
No, that can't be right.

179
00:12:07,950 --> 00:12:09,660
It's Griffith...

180
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:11,790
The Griffith we both know...

181
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:14,620
What I did wouldn't
be enough to bring Griffith down.

182
00:12:15,630 --> 00:12:17,460
There's no way, don't you see?

183
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:21,090
Really... You're just a hopeless fool...

184
00:12:21,090 --> 00:12:22,090
...aren't you?

185
00:12:27,010 --> 00:12:28,850
I told you this once before!

186
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:31,310
Those striving to achieve greatness...

187
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:33,810
...must also carry a burden
greater than anyone else.

188
00:12:34,690 --> 00:12:35,520
Griffith...

189
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:38,110
...had to become stronger than the rest.

190
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,530
But...

191
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,940
Griffith is not a god...

192
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:45,860
Ideals and dreams alone
aren't enough to satisfy a man's heart.

193
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,950
It was you who came
along and made Griffith weak!

194
00:12:51,450 --> 00:12:54,620
Griffith can't go on without you!

195
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:06,090
Impossible...

196
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:08,050
You could've dodged that attack easily...

197
00:13:10,850 --> 00:13:12,520
What was I supposed to do?

198
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:18,860
L-Let go.

199
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:22,690
I did what I had to do, just like Griffith.

200
00:13:23,190 --> 00:13:24,860
That's enough. Let go.

201
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:27,660
All I did was what needed to be done.

202
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,700
How else
was I supposed to handle it?

203
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:33,160
Let go.

204
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,120
All right, just let go!

205
00:13:44,210 --> 00:13:45,340
I know.

206
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,880
I understand.

207
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:48,840
The truth is...

208
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:51,810
...you're right.

209
00:13:53,270 --> 00:13:56,100
But I can't take it...

210
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,730
I can't bear it...

211
00:14:02,570 --> 00:14:07,990
If only I could change the way my
heart feels, it'd be so much easier...

212
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:10,570
I'm not stupid...

213
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:13,580
I know that the quickest path...

214
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:16,620
...to the throne of Midland is
by marrying Princess Charlotte.

215
00:14:17,370 --> 00:14:18,960
I knew that all along.

216
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:24,750
And I knew that if it was up to Griffith,
that would be the path he would take.

217
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:28,630
Somehow, I thought I could handle it.

218
00:14:29,090 --> 00:14:33,220
Even if I couldn't stand by
Griffith's side as a woman...

219
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:34,970
...I could at least stay near him as his sword...

220
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:38,390
That's what I wanted to believe.

221
00:14:41,310 --> 00:14:44,270
But the day you left...

222
00:14:45,110 --> 00:14:46,990
...it finally became clear to me.

223
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:53,740
The days that I had spent by
Griffith's side were a thing of the past...

224
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:57,950
My dream had already ended.

225
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:03,460
The reason why I've kept us together...

226
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:06,130
...even if it's just a phantom hope...

227
00:15:06,130 --> 00:15:09,550
...is because unless I cling on
to them, I may lose my self.

228
00:15:10,430 --> 00:15:13,010
But it doesn't matter now.

229
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:16,510
I can never be the woman of his life...

230
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:18,980
...or something that he treasures.

231
00:15:19,810 --> 00:15:22,480
Preserving the crumbling dream of a man...

232
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:25,320
...whom I don't even know is alive or not...

233
00:15:26,150 --> 00:15:28,280
It's too much... for me...

234
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:31,360
I'm so tired...

235
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:33,660
You take care of the rest.

236
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:34,280
Casca?

237
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:03,270
Damn it!

238
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:04,770
What are you thinking?

239
00:16:04,770 --> 00:16:05,610
Listen to me!

240
00:16:05,610 --> 00:16:07,690
Don't go near that cliff again!

241
00:16:07,690 --> 00:16:10,320
I can't afford to be
dragged down with you again!

242
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,190
Understood?

243
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:13,660
Fool.

244
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:15,120
What?

245
00:16:25,130 --> 00:16:27,540
You're always getting hurt somewhere...

246
00:16:28,550 --> 00:16:31,510
Always shedding blood because of me...

247
00:16:32,050 --> 00:16:33,010
You...

248
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:36,390
Fool.

249
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:39,180
Such a fool.

250
00:16:57,370 --> 00:17:00,490
The day you left...
That was when I first realized...

251
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:05,920
After Griffith's first defeat at your hand,
he was on his knees, devastated...

252
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:08,750
But you were the one
I couldn't take my eyes off of...

253
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:12,300
As you walked away without
so much as a backward glance...

254
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,970
I didn't want to accept
those feelings of mine.

255
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:21,260
Because if I did, everything in my life
since the moment I met Griffith...

256
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:23,640
...would have all been a lie.

257
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:27,770
I've always lived true to my heart...

258
00:17:28,310 --> 00:17:31,020
That was the one thing
I could be proud of.

259
00:17:32,190 --> 00:17:35,490
Because that was
the gift Griffith gave to me...

260
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:37,610
But...

261
00:17:44,450 --> 00:17:45,960
I can change...

262
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:51,250
There just might be a place
for me inside this man's soul...

263
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:55,470
Instead of only taking...

264
00:17:56,130 --> 00:17:58,930
I might be able to give
something back this time.

265
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:07,310
Guts...

266
00:18:07,730 --> 00:18:09,560
Why don't you stay with us?

267
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:14,480
We'll rescue Griffith, and then
we'll all be together, like before...

268
00:18:15,570 --> 00:18:16,650
I can't.

269
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,450
I just want to put things
back together. That's all.

270
00:18:21,490 --> 00:18:26,910
I'll stay till we rescue Griffith and get
the Band of the Hawk back on its feet...

271
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:28,670
But that's it...

272
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:30,580
I must continue my journey...

273
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,300
I'm through with drawing
my sword for others...

274
00:18:34,670 --> 00:18:36,550
And I won't hang on
to someone else's dream anymore.

275
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:39,970
From now on,
I'm going to fight my own battles.

276
00:18:49,890 --> 00:18:51,560
How noble...

277
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,940
I'm very impressed...

278
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:57,990
You're just like Griffith!

279
00:18:58,650 --> 00:18:59,780
Your dream is everything to you!

280
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:01,530
Everything's always about you!

281
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:03,990
It doesn't matter to you if I'm here or not!

282
00:19:04,740 --> 00:19:05,540
Hey!

283
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:06,740
Just go!

284
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:09,790
Go off and end up dead
in a ditch somewhere for all I care...

285
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:13,630
Go off and die with your precious sword!

286
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:17,960
Come with me.

287
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,050
What?

288
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:21,630
You heard me... Come with me.

289
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:27,220
I don't know what the future will bring...

290
00:19:27,970 --> 00:19:31,640
All I know is that I haven't
held you long enough yet.

291
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:33,060
Fool!

292
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:35,060
I want to make love to you a hundred...

293
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:37,230
No, a thousand times more...

294
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,490
That's how I feel right now.

295
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,280
You fool.

296
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:21,570
What the...

297
00:20:56,150 --> 00:21:00,110
If it weren't for my arm,
I could have gone with you guys.

298
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,570
Don't be disappointed.

299
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:05,660
You'll be the first one to get a hug
from Griffith when he comes back.

300
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:08,160
I'm counting on you, Guts.

301
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:10,490
Promise you'll bring him back safe.

302
00:21:10,490 --> 00:21:11,330
Yeah.

303
00:21:11,830 --> 00:21:13,160
On your horses!

304
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:23,300
We're splitting up into two units,
and we'll be taking separate action.

305
00:21:23,670 --> 00:21:26,630
Griffith's rescue unit shall now set off!

306
00:21:26,630 --> 00:21:28,010
Let's go, boss!

307
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:34,310
Rescue unit...

308
00:21:34,310 --> 00:21:36,310
Depart for Midland!

309
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

310
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

311
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

312
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

313
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

314
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

315
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

316
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

317
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

318
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

319
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

